// A negated obligation lapses with the parent too: the negations are pushed to the formulas
// without temporal operators first, so !(F error) is G !error, and lets the machine disappear.
// The assertion holds, and the model has a trace.

machine ?
  ctx
    error ?
    [ !(F error) ]
    assert [ (G !error) <=> !(F error) ]
    assert [ !(X error) <=> X !error ]
    assert [ !(error U !error) <=> (error W (!error && error)) ]

[ initially machine ]
[ initially (X no machine) ]
